167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:.github/workflows/lens-dev.yml:40:          repository: BerriAI/lens
167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:.github/workflows/lens-dev.yml:113:          repository: BerriAI/lens
167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:docs/lens-independent-deployment.md:80:The earlier [Helm ownership rehearsal](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/48758d944504d0960d1b920cacf2566d5b9206c7/docs/extraction/evidence/helm/adoption.json) used local image `sha256:2b5b6bee2d3cb08f54271c2ba71ccceb3a22d41678a788c2d6b4b19781cfe66b` on Kubernetes 1.35.0 with Helm 3.19.0. It transferred the existing resources to a separate release, removed the old release, changed replica count, rolled back and restarted Lens and ClickHouse. Trace, dataset revision/export, session, credentials and resource identities survived. This proves resource adoption, not compatibility between two published runtime versions
167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:docs/lens-independent-deployment.md:82:The later [Argo rehearsal](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/48758d944504d0960d1b920cacf2566d5b9206c7/docs/extraction/evidence/helm/argo-successor-final-image.json) used ops commit `8e541e2fa89f41cd24c7fc4f22d5b325e39a8e5e` and Argo 3.3.8. It upgraded a retained populated baseline to Lens commit `70c2d61e36503116241dcc2fbf5f51ed69cbf430`, image `sha256:6592e532802c79b08bb45a26e7a332d1711b9f862984e7c7d45702fad6d060ef`, and rolled back to the distinct `b0f3d5b` baseline. Both transitions reached Synced/Healthy and retained data, credentials and resource identities. A provider-backed investigation completed on the final image and remained readable after rollback. Wrong-digest and zero-replica checks failed as expected
167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:docs/lens-independent-deployment.md:84:The [populated migration and cold restore](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/48758d944504d0960d1b920cacf2566d5b9206c7/docs/extraction/evidence/populated-migration.json) used Lens commit `105e7b0`. The [final packaged importer check](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/48758d944504d0960d1b920cacf2566d5b9206c7/docs/extraction/evidence/importer-final-image.json) separately qualified `70c2d61`, including all eight source groups, read-only source access, invalid-source refusal, exact scopes and credential hashes, dataset revisions and idempotent repeat import. These use representative local data
167c553aeb3679bb52a6e5dc0b8d0f8cbbcfaaf3:docs/lens-independent-deployment.md:86:The [final candidate chart qualification](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/9e4974603aa1e3f638ebe93284eb309110dc5ec8/docs/extraction/evidence/helm/gateway-candidate-final.json), from [run 37924154315](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/actions/runs/37924154315), reused ten verified production-image builds, with Lens current `70c2d61` and baseline `0b8e2c2`, and gateway current `d83eab0` and baseline `a41b93a`. Both gateway chart families passed fresh installation, trace ingestion, Lens-only upgrade and image rollback, gateway-only upgrade with unchanged Lens pods, restart, external Lens reads/writes and disabled behavior. The gateway upgrades used Helm-owned migration Jobs and verified their successful replacement
